      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:10:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Breaking Encapsulation and OS Primitive Safety**\nIn the `ft98xx_alg_before` setup function, you clear the algorithm\u0027s private data using `memset`:\n\n```c\n\tif (fixture-\u003ealg \u0026\u0026 fixture-\u003ealg-\u003edata) {\n\t\tmemset(fixture-\u003ealg-\u003edata, 0, sizeof(struct ft_libfp_data));\n\t}\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** Bypassing abstraction in a test suite is sometimes necessary, but resetting a state structure strictly via `memset` is risky in Zephyr. If `struct ft_libfp_data` contains any initialized Zephyr OS primitives (like a `k_mutex`, `k_sem`, or `k_work`), zeroing them out will corrupt those objects and cause hardware faults during test execution.\n* **Suggestion:** If possible, rely on `fingerprint_algorithm_exit()` to cleanly reset the internal state. If you absolutely must clear it manually here, ensure (and perhaps document) that `struct ft_libfp_data` is strictly POD (Plain Old Data) with no OS-level synchronization primitives.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "d3f21f0a98d57f63bb35c4046000eea813f4fbc8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
